WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.899 --> 00:00:11.299
BEN: Hello, Little Fox readers, and welcome back to People in the News . Today Olivia is going

2
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:16.049
to tell you about the American actor Johnny Depp. He's one of the most famous—and unusual—actors in the

3
00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:20.878
world. OLIVIA: That's right, Ben. Johnny was born on June 9, 1963. His father was a civil engineer,

4
00:00:20.879 --> 00:00:26.375
and his mom worked as a waitress. Johnny was the youngest of four children, and life at

5
00:00:26.376 --> 00:00:31.119
home was often noisy and unpredictable. His parents, who later got divorced, frequently argued. Because his family also

6
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:37.523
moved around a lot, Johnny often changed schools and had trouble making friends. He's admitted to many interviewers

7
00:00:37.524 --> 00:00:42.266
that he was a bit of an oddball as a kid. He mostly kept to himself, spending his

8
00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:49.026
time drawing, reading comic books, and watching horror movies. When Johnny turned 12, his mother bought him something

9
00:00:49.027 --> 00:00:53.849
that quickly turned into his passion—a guitar. Johnny practiced constantly, locking himself in his bedroom for hours. As

10
00:00:53.850 --> 00:01:00.857
a teenager Johnny often acted out, getting into trouble for smoking and even experimenting with drugs. At

11
00:01:00.858 --> 00:01:08.095
around age 16, he decided to drop out of high school to focus on his band, The Kids.

12
00:01:08.096 --> 00:01:13.585
In 1983 Johnny and The Kids moved to California, hoping to get a record deal. The band didn't

13
00:01:13.586 --> 00:01:21.237
have much success, however, and Johnny soon found himself living in a friend's car and selling pens over

14
00:01:21.238 --> 00:01:28.721
the phone as a way to make money. Johnny had never considered a career as an actor until

15
00:01:28.722 --> 00:01:35.307
a friend saw potential in Johnny and introduced him to a Hollywood agent, who helped him find acting

16
00:01:35.308 --> 00:01:44.809
jobs. By 1984 Johnny had landed his first role in a Hollywood movie, A Nightmare on Elm Street

17
00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:55.454
. The movie was very successful at the box office, but it didn't make Johnny a star.

18
00:01:55.455 --> 00:02:03.034
Nor did it change Johnny's feelings about acting. He still saw himself as a musician, not a Hollywood

19
00:02:03.035 --> 00:02:08.620
actor. Then Johnny got a part in Platoon , a movie about the war in Vietnam. Before filming

20
00:02:08.621 --> 00:02:12.195
began, the actors were required to attend military boot camp and sleep in the jungle under harsh conditions.

21
00:02:12.196 --> 00:02:16.945
They had to eat military rations and take turns sitting up all night, watching for any dangers. Johnny's

22
00:02:16.946 --> 00:02:22.427
role in Platoon was small, but its demands taught him something important—he enjoyed taking on challenging roles. Soon

23
00:02:22.428 --> 00:02:30.682
Johnny was taking acting lessons and working closely with acting coaches, determined to learn more about the craft.

24
00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:37.093
In 1987 Johnny was offered the chance to star in 21 Jump Street —a TV show about

25
00:02:37.094 --> 00:02:45.420
undercover police officers in a high school. At first Johnny turned down the role because he didn’t want

26
00:02:45.421 --> 00:02:53.738
to commit himself to a job that could go on for years and years. Later he changed his

27
00:02:53.739 --> 00:03:03.408
mind, though, because he needed the money. Soon the show was a big hit, especially among teenage girls.

28
00:03:03.409 --> 00:03:10.891
BEN: Wow, he must have been thrilled by all the attention! OLIVIA: It was actually just the opposite,

29
00:03:10.892 --> 00:03:14.713
Ben. Johnny was miserable because the role didn't involve much skill or acting ability; it was just about

30
00:03:14.714 --> 00:03:19.806
being a famous TV star. In fact, he even destroyed a 21 Jump Street billboard because he

31
00:03:19.807 --> 00:03:23.714
couldn't stand seeing his own picture on it! After four seasons he quit 21 Jump Street to concentrate

32
00:03:23.715 --> 00:03:26.560
on acting projects that challenged him more. One of these was Edward Scissorhands , an unusual movie about

33
00:03:26.561 --> 00:03:34.869
a lonely boy with scissors for hands. Johnny threw himself into the leading role, and when the film

34
00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:42.711
was released, he received rave reviews for his sensitive portrayal of Edward. After Edward Scissorhands Johnny was offered

35
00:03:42.712 --> 00:03:49.440
plenty of other movie roles, but he turned down most of them, taking only parts that involved quirky

36
00:03:49.441 --> 00:03:56.773
or interesting characters. And he prepared for these parts in an unusual way—by painting portraits of the characters

37
00:03:56.774 --> 00:04:06.267
to help him bring them to life. The role that made Johnny a superstar was, of course,

38
00:04:06.268 --> 00:04:17.192
Captain Jack Sparrow in Pirates of the Caribbean: The Curse of the Black Pearl . At first many

39
00:04:17.193 --> 00:04:25.255
people had low expectations for the movie, which was originally based on a theme park ride. During production,

40
00:04:25.256 --> 00:04:34.901
executives grew even more concerned about the film because Johnny was playing Sparrow in an odd way, as

41
00:04:34.902 --> 00:04:42.243
if the pirate captain were slightly crazy. The executives tried to get Johnny to change this approach, but

42
00:04:42.244 --> 00:04:53.064
Johnny continued to follow his own vision. Later, when the movie came out, fans and critics definitely showed

43
00:04:53.065 --> 00:04:59.237
their appreciation for Johnny's acting—the movie was a hit at the box office, and he received several awards

44
00:04:59.238 --> 00:05:13.385
for his outstanding and unusual performance. Since then some of Johnny's best-known roles have been in movies

45
00:05:13.386 --> 00:05:18.290
for kids. He's played Willie Wonka in Charlie and the Chocolate Factory and the Mad Hatter in Alice

46
00:05:18.291 --> 00:05:24.700
in Wonderland . Johnny has told many interviewers that he doesn’t really care if his movies are huge

47
00:05:24.701 --> 00:05:34.130
hits or huge flops, and he doesn’t take his fame very seriously. He rarely even watches his own

48
00:05:34.131 --> 00:05:41.368
movies! Instead the thing that matters most to him is his family. Today he spends lots of time

49
00:05:41.369 --> 00:05:49.528
with his kids, both in France and on a secluded Caribbean island where he owns a house. When

50
00:05:49.529 --> 00:05:55.113
he's not making movies, he still enjoys drawing and playing his guitar. BEN: Johnny Depp sounds like

51
00:05:55.114 --> 00:05:59.339
a pretty unique actor, Olivia. OLIVIA: He is, Ben. He's a famous movie star now, but he's basically

52
00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:10.271
the same person he always was—a quiet outsider who follows his own artistic vision. BEN: Thanks for that

53
00:06:10.272 --> 00:06:20.586
interesting report. We'll see you next week, Little Fox readers, when we meet another person in the news!

